FILED s543m (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-27), from the reviewing session's review of s543m (F4; m-11 row 7).  PRE-EXISTING: base 9a3ce86f the same.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 | ./runpcl; scratch/s543m/p11/rows.pl prog 4):
    my $f = "/tmp/x.$$"; sub mk { open my $t, ">", $f or die; print $t "hdata"; $t } sub sz { my $s = -s $f; unlink $f; $s // "none" }
    my %h; sub d2 { return delete $h{fh} } $h{fh} = mk(); d2(); print "a ", sz(), "\n";
    sub d3 { my $s = shift; return delete $s->{fh} } my $o = { fh => mk() }; d3($o); print "b ", sz(), "\n";
    $h{fh} = mk(); my $k = d2(); print "c ", sz(), "\n";     # control: the caller KEEPS it (perl 0)
perl: a 5 / b 5 / c 0.  PCL (base and tree): a 0 / b 0 / c 0.

SAME PLACE AS THE :tail WRAP? NO.  The tail wrap is `Parser2::_lower_expr_stmt` (a block's last EXPRESSION statement, `$tail_ctx` 'inherit': `(p-flush-dropped-value FORM :tail)`); a `return` statement is lowered by the break-statement path (`p-return` / `p-tail-value` of `_lower_expr($expr, $stmt, 'inherit', 1)`, Parser2 near "A returned call must see the CALLER's context").  Direction: that path asks `Pl::Stmt::drop_value_shape` of the return's expression and wraps the returned form the same way (`:tail` outside eval text) -- one helper for the wrap shared by both paths (rule 11), not a copy.  The `p-tail-value` / `p-return` value and context must stay byte-identical in meaning (s543j: a comma list in the caller's context).
